{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b5aa2f165d7affb4","name":"card_unit_me_bf_109_brothers","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/BrothersInArms/units/card_unit_me_bf_109_brothers","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"ME BF 109 G","text":"Pincer: When this unit attacks and destroys a unit, gain a kredit and draw a card.","flavorText":"The Messerschmitt Bf 109 G was a German fighter aircraft that was primarily used during WWII. It was an improved version of the earlier Bf 109 F model and was introduced into service in 1942. The Bf 109 G was powered by a Daimler-Benz DB 605 engine, and a GM-1 nitrous oxide power boost, which produced up to 1,475 horsepower. It had a top speed of around 685 km/h (426 mph) and a range of approximately 850 km (528 miles). The armament of the Bf 109 G variant typically included one MG 151/20 20mm cannon and two 7.92mm MG 17 machine guns. Some later variants of the Bf 109 G also included additional armament, such as rockets or an underwing gondola cannon kit. One of the notable features of the Bf 109 G was its improved aerodynamics and performance, which made it faster and more agile than earlier versions. It was also equipped with advanced radio and navigation equipment, which made it well-suited for both bomber escort and ground-attack missions. The Bf 109 G saw extensive service on all fronts of the war and was flown by some of the top German aces of the war, including Erich Hartmann and Gerhard Barkhorn. It remained in service until the end of the war, and over 33,000 Bf 109s of all variants were produced, making it one of the most successful fighter aircraft in history.","faction":"Germany","type":"fighter","rarity":"Rare","cost":3,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_me_bf_109_brothers","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_me_bf_109_brothers_title","SourceString":"ME BF 109 G","LocalizedString":"ME BF 109 G"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighte